From: DroidDeck
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: keep the game's keyboard focus under Steam's overlay

The Steam client opens its Quick Access Menu and Steam menu over a game by setting
STEAM_OVERLAY 1 and STEAM_INPUT_FOCUS 1 on its window. Mode 1 moves X keyboard focus to the
overlay, so the game's window gets FocusOut: wine moves the foreground to the desktop, a fullscreen
game deactivates and minimizes itself (WM_CHANGE_STATE IconicState), and it stops rendering behind
the menu - frozen, all threads asleep, until the menu closes (Alan Wake's American Nightmare,
Proton Experimental ARM64). On a Steam Deck the game runs on behind the menu.

Mode 2 already means "input to the overlay, keyboard focus stays on the focus window". Treat
Steam's own overlay taking input in mode 1 the same way at the three places mode 2 is honoured.
The overlay's input does not need X keyboard focus: the controller drives it through Steam Input.
Measured by rewriting the property to 2 by hand: the game kept running behind the menu and the
controller still moved only the menu.

With the game keeping focus, the pointer resets gamescope makes when input moves to Steam (warp
to the centre, park in the corner) and back (warp to the centre) reached it as a sudden mouse
move: a mouse-look camera spun every time the menu opened and closed. Skip them while Steam's
overlay opens over a game that keeps focus, and as it closes - by then the overlay has dropped its
STEAM_INPUT_FOCUS, so whether the opening kept focus is remembered.

diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index 372a82c..3fab3c6 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -1321,6 +1321,22 @@ window_is_steam( steamcompmgr_win_t *w )
 	return w && ( w->isSteamLegacyBigPicture || w->appID == 769 );
 }
 
+// Whether keyboard focus stays on the focus window while this window has input focus.
+// STEAM_INPUT_FOCUS 2 asks for that. The Steam client also opens its Quick Access Menu and Steam
+// menu over a game with 1, which moves X keyboard focus to the overlay: wine then deactivates the
+// game, a fullscreen game minimizes itself, and it froze behind the menu instead of running on as
+// on a Steam Deck. The overlay's own input does not need X keyboard focus (the controller drives
+// it through Steam Input), so Steam's overlay keeps the game's keyboard focus too.
+static bool
+window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus( steamcompmgr_win_t *w )
+{
+	if ( !w )
+		return false;
+	if ( w->inputFocusMode == 2 )
+		return true;
+	return w->inputFocusMode == 1 && w->isOverlay && window_is_steam( w );
+}
+
 static bool
 window_is_vr_scene_app( steamcompmgr_win_t *w )
 {
@@ -4728,7 +4744,7 @@ void xwayland_ctx_t::DetermineAndApplyFocus( const std::vector< steamcompmgr_win
 
 	if ( gamescope::VirtualConnectorIsSingleOutput() )
 	{
-		if ( inputFocus && inputFocus->inputFocusMode == 2 )
+		if ( window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus( inputFocus ) )
 			keyboardFocusWin = ctx->focus.focusWindow;
 	}
 	else
@@ -4834,12 +4850,26 @@ void xwayland_ctx_t::DetermineAndApplyFocus( const std::vector< steamcompmgr_win
 		if ( ctx->focus.inputFocusWindow != inputFocus ||
 			 ctx->focus.inputFocusMode != inputFocus->inputFocusMode )
 		{
+			// Steam's overlay opening over a game, or closing again, while the game keeps keyboard focus
+			// (window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus): the game is still taking input, so a pointer warp
+			// reaches it as a sudden mouse move - the camera of a mouse-look game spun as the Quick
+			// Access Menu opened and as it closed. The overlay is driven by the controller and the
+			// cursor is hidden, so leave the pointer where it is. Closing, the overlay has already
+			// dropped its STEAM_INPUT_FOCUS, so whether the opening kept focus is remembered.
+			static bool s_bOverlayKeptGameFocus = false;
+			bool bOverlayKeepsGameFocus = window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus( inputFocus ) &&
+				ctx->focus.focusWindow && !window_is_steam( ctx->focus.focusWindow );
+			bool bSkipPointerReset = bOverlayKeepsGameFocus || s_bOverlayKeptGameFocus;
+			s_bOverlayKeptGameFocus = bOverlayKeepsGameFocus;
+
 			// If the window doesn't want focus when hidden, move it away
 			// as we are going to hide it straight after.
 			// otherwise, if we switch from wanting it to not
 			// (steam -> game)
 			// put us back in the centre of the screen.
-			if (window_wants_no_focus_when_mouse_hidden(inputFocus))
+			if ( bSkipPointerReset )
+				;
+			else if (window_wants_no_focus_when_mouse_hidden(inputFocus))
 				ctx->focus.bResetToCorner = true;
 			else if ( window_wants_no_focus_when_mouse_hidden(inputFocus) != window_wants_no_focus_when_mouse_hidden(ctx->focus.inputFocusWindow) )
 				ctx->focus.bResetToCenter = true;
@@ -5340,7 +5370,7 @@ determine_and_apply_focus( global_focus_t *pFocus )
 		pFocus->inputFocusMode = pFocus->inputFocusWindow->inputFocusMode;
 
 	if ( gamescope::VirtualConnectorIsSingleOutput() &&
-	     pFocus->inputFocusMode == 2 )
+	     window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus( pFocus->inputFocusWindow ) )
 	{
 		pFocus->keyboardFocusWindow = pFocus->overrideWindow
 			? pFocus->overrideWindow
@@ -6485,7 +6515,7 @@ handle_wl_surface_id(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, steamcompmgr_win_t *w, uint32_t surfac
 		steamcompmgr_win_t *keyboardFocusWindow = pCurrentFocus->inputFocusWindow;
 
 		if ( gamescope::VirtualConnectorIsSingleOutput() &&
-		     keyboardFocusWindow && keyboardFocusWindow->inputFocusMode == 2 )
+		     window_keeps_game_keyboard_focus( keyboardFocusWindow ) )
 			keyboardFocusWindow = pCurrentFocus->focusWindow;
 
 		if ( w == keyboardFocusWindow )
